maak (1.4.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * maak can drive `zig build`: (maak zig) is a new module -- built the way
    (maak cargo) is -- providing zig-argv and zig-build-argv, the usual steps,
    the direct compiler commands, zig-fmt, zig-fetch and zig-version, all
    re-exported by (maak maak).  Zig keeps the dependency graph and maak builds
    the command line, so the argv is pure and --dry-run and --plan show it
    without Zig installed.  zig-build-clean removes a local prefix and refuses
    to leave the project; zig-build-uninstall names the step Zig has not
    implemented rather than running a build that panics.  MAAK_ZIG selects the
    program.  The README's diagram is redrawn and answers to a dark colour
    scheme as well as a light one.

