maak (1.2.3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Test and manifest only; no library code, command line or generated script
    changed.  The Bash completion cases failed in a build with "complete:
    command not found", because the bash a Guix shell hands you is
    bash-minimal, built without readline and therefore without programmable
    completion at all.  The manifest names the full bash now, and the spec
    asks first and passes those cases unrun where the shell cannot complete.

